      "committer": {
        "name": "dylanoliverdo-coder",
        "email": "265406556+dylanoliverdo-coder@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T23:18:28Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): the field ceiling bounds a chord's travel, not the tool's own footprint (#4079)\n\nSdfField::subtract_batch refused a chord when its clipped swept window\npassed MAX_CELLS_PER_MOVE (1 << 22). A wide tool's own footprint can pass\nthat count, so a 1 mm move of a 50.8 mm flat tool at 0.254 mm cells was\nrefused, and segmenting could not help. The column engine cuts it.\n\nThe ceiling now bounds the cells of the clipped window beyond the window\nof the same solid at rest at the chord's start (Sweep::rest_window, the\nsame reach, padding and clipping). A short move of any tool passes. A long\nchord still refuses with the same advice, and segmenting always brings it\nunder the ceiling. The lathe sweep has no rest window and keeps the old\nbound. The f32 cut twin keeps its own value (follow-up).\n\nPins (crates/sim/tests/field_wide_tool.rs): the 1 mm move cuts on both\nengines (fails on the old code: refused); a 120 mm chord of the same tool\nstill refuses and its 5 mm pieces cut. The unpayable-window pin in\nstock_sdf_cut still refuses.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
